@startuml state-quick-paste-input
!include _style.iuml
title Quick Paste keyboard focus and input (PasteWindow + QuickPasteController)

[*] --> ShortcutMode : ShowForPaste

state "Shortcut mode\n(root grid focused)" as ShortcutMode {
  ShortcutMode : letter/digit -> SingleKey -> paste, or error tone
  ShortcutMode : Up/Down -> move highlight (wraps)
  ShortcutMode : Enter -> CommitHighlighted -> paste
}
state "Search box" as Search {
  Search : letters filter tree and both lists
  Search : Up -> caret to start, Down -> caret to end
}
state "Tree" as Tree {
  Tree : arrows move/expand, Enter or double-click -> paste
  Tree : right-click -> Paste / Paste As
}
state "Alt held: multi-key entry" as Multi {
  Multi : TypeMulti(c) narrows the multi-key list
  Multi : '_' (Alt+Shift+-) marks plain text
  Multi : Alt+Backspace -> Backspace
  Multi : Up/Down -> MoveMultiHighlight
  Multi : Enter -> CommitMulti -> paste
}

ShortcutMode --> Search : Tab / Ctrl+F / click
Search --> Tree : Tab, or Down at end of text
Tree --> ShortcutMode : Tab
Search --> ShortcutMode : Esc (clears the filter)
Tree --> Search : Esc, or a printable key (typed there)
ShortcutMode --> Multi : Alt down / AltDown()
Search --> Multi : Alt down
Tree --> Multi : Alt down
Multi --> ShortcutMode : Alt up with nothing typed\n/ previous tab back
Multi --> [*] : Alt up with a key typed -> paste
Multi --> ShortcutMode : Alt+Esc (low-level hook) / CancelEntry
ShortcutMode --> [*] : Esc -> hide (kept warm)
ShortcutMode --> [*] : paste -> window closed (destroyed)
@enduml
